## Codex in ChatGPT Business: seats, a shared pool and admin controls

{% logo src="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/devanshug2307/agentskills-blog-content/main/images/is-codex-free-pricing-and-limits/logos/codex-business.png" name="Codex Business" size=40 /%}

**What it is.** ChatGPT Business gives teams Codex under the same plan structure, with workspace administration. The pricing page's usage table has a "Standard Business" column whose message ranges match Plus. A cached copy of OpenAI's chatgpt.com/codex/pricing page (seen in search results, not re-opened as a page) mentions a $20 Business plan and a $100 Business plan, which tell us there are at least two Business tiers. A third-party tracker reports $20 per seat billed annually and $25 monthly for two or more seats; we could not confirm those two numbers on OpenAI's own page today.

**Who it is for.** Small teams that want central billing, admin control over models and cloud access, and a shared credit option.

**Key features.**
- Workspace admins can set the starting model, reasoning level, speed and Fast mode behavior from Workspace settings, per the help center.
- Role-based access control for Codex, and Codex usage appears in the Compliance API.
- Plugins can be set to Available or Installed per role.
- Codex cloud is available to eligible Business accounts, subject to workspace settings.

**Pros**
- Admin visibility and controls that individual plans lack.
- Shared usage model with the Plus numbers as a baseline.

**Cons**
- Exact per-seat prices are not stated on the page we could fetch.
- On Business and Enterprise with credits, usage can be billed in dollars instead of credits (OpenAI says Enterprise token-based agreements bill Codex in USD).

**Benefits for your use case.** If three developers each buy Plus, you get three separate allowances and no admin view. Business is the route when someone needs to control access and models centrally.

**Pricing.** See OpenAI's Business pricing for your region; the Codex pricing page references $20 and $100 Business tiers. **Free tier:** none. **Limits:** same estimates as Plus for Standard Business.

**Standout use case.** A team that wants to pilot Codex with a managed model list and cloud access policy.

**Skip it if** you are one person, or you do not need admin controls.

